=You are tailoring ONE resume for Gurkirat Singh Wadhawan for this specific job.

JOB:
Title: {{ $json.title }}
Company: {{ $json.company }}
Location: {{ $json.location }}
Job Description: {{ JSON.stringify(($('Webhook').first().json.body.jobs.find(j => j.job_id === $json.job_id) || {}).description || '') }}

CANDIDATE MASTER RESUME (JSON):
{{ JSON.stringify($('Webhook').first().json.body.master_resume) }}

The master resume's "experience" entries each contain a pool of bullets, each tagged with the role families it's strongest for, plus a "skills_keyword_bank" of real, verified keywords/tools grouped by category.

1. Select bullets across ALL experience entries, weighted by relevance, using these MINIMUM per-employer counts (never go below these, even for weaker-fit employers -- pull straight from that employer's bullet pool if needed to hit the minimum): Allegis Group >= 6, KPMG >= 4, Career Intelligence Platform (personal project, in progress) >= 3, Thrivent Federal Credit Union >= 2 (its full pool). Give MORE than the minimum (up to that employer's full bullet pool) to whichever employer/role is most relevant to this job. This resume is allowed to run to 2 pages -- prioritize concrete, substantive coverage of each employer over fitting one page.
2. ORDER the selected bullets within each experience entry from most to least relevant to THIS job's description.
3. Lightly reword bullets to mirror the job description's exact terminology and verb choice, only swapping to honest synonyms for the same scope of involvement -- never implying more ownership, seniority, or credit than the source bullet describes. Weave in exact-match keywords from skills_keyword_bank where genuinely reflected in that bullet's work.
4. You have full freedom over structure and presentation: which summary_variant to use, which skills to list and in what order, how many bullets per employer, and how bullets are worded -- all aggressively tailored to mirror this job description's language and priorities.
4a. Write for impact, not just accuracy -- lead each bullet with the business outcome or result, tools/technologies second. Vary action verbs across bullets.
4b. When two bullets from the same employer are similarly relevant, prefer the one carrying a real quantified metric for the higher/earlier position.
5. HARD LIMIT: never change, invent, or round a quantified metric to match numbers in the job description. Metrics must stay exactly as given in the source bullet. Do not introduce a tool, technology, or claim not in the source bullet or skills_keyword_bank.

RETURN ONLY VALID JSON. No markdown, no explanations, no code fences.

Required Output Format:
{
  "tailored_summary": "string",
  "tailored_skills": ["string", "string"],
  "tailored_resume_bullets": [
    { "company": "string", "bullets": ["string", "string"] }
  ]
}

Rules:
- tailored_resume_bullets must include one entry per experience entry in the master resume.
- tailored_summary: pick the summary_variant that best fits this job (or lightly blend/reword two variants).
- tailored_skills: a reordered, job-relevant subset of skills_keyword_bank (only real entries from it, most relevant first).
- Return only valid JSON, a single object (not an array).

